Vendored third-party dependency
===============================

  Library:  poseidon (Noir)
  Upstream: https://github.com/noir-lang/poseidon
  Tag:      v0.2.0
  Commit:   4bc50d88dd8d94a00a95730fd76501e676417abf
  License:  Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE)

Vendored verbatim at the commit above; no modifications to the source. Only the
build/CI scaffolding of the upstream repository is omitted (workflows, package
manifests, benchmark scripts, TypeScript oracle server), none of which is
compiled by nargo.

Why vendored
------------
The circuits previously depended on this library through a mutable Git tag
(`tag = "v0.2.0"`). A tag can be moved to a different commit by the upstream
maintainer, and nargo has no commit-`rev` key and writes no lockfile, so nothing
recorded the resolved commit. A rebuild could therefore fetch different library
source from unchanged repository source, producing a different ACIR and a
different verification key. Vendoring by `path` is the only way to freeze the
exact source in-manifest. See the OpenZeppelin audit finding N-06.

Updating
--------
Do not edit these files in place. To move to a new upstream version, replace the
directory wholesale from the new commit, update this NOTICE, regenerate the
circuits that depend on it, and re-baseline their committed artifacts and the
tests that use them. Changing this library changes the verification key of every
circuit that imports it — currently `identity` and `tornado`.
